codex
Ran four experiments and all were `discard`, so the branch is reset cleanly to the current best commit `207179d` on `research-loops/jul13`.

Current best remains `val_bpb = 1.208927` from `lower matrix LR further with earlier cooldown`. New results recorded in `memory/results.tsv` were:
- `1.222462` for `keep token embeddings fp32, cast lookups to bf16`
- `1.211339` for `keep 10% late LR floor for embedding and lm head`
- `1.210042` for `halve sequence length to 1024 and double device batch`
- `1.213788` for `use 1536-token sequences with near-matched total batch`

The closest miss was the `1024`-token run, so that throughput/context tradeoff looks more promising than the LR-floor or embedding-precision changes.
